// F is true (target is reached, trivially, in one step) but G F is false in every mode
// (target can never be revisited after that single step) -- proves the Buchi operators
// are not just inheriting the reachability operators' answer.

// RESULT: true
<<p1>> sure [ F x=1 ]

// RESULT: false
<<p1>> sure [ G F x=1 ]

// RESULT: false
<<p1>> almost [ G F x=1 ]

// RESULT: false
<<p1>> limit [ G F x=1 ]
